#: ../portal/src/routes/faq/+page.svelte
msgid "Nocturne runs in Docker, so any system that runs Docker (Linux, Windows, macOS) can host it. For a single user, 2 GB of RAM and one CPU core will run it, though 4 GB is more comfortable because PostgreSQL uses the spare memory as disk cache. Allow 10 GB of storage, most of which is the container images. For families or several sites, 4 GB or more is recommended. You also need a domain name pointed at the server."
msgstr "Nocturne runs in Docker, so any system that runs Docker (Linux, Windows, macOS) can host it. For a single user, 2 GB of RAM and one CPU core will run it, though 4 GB is more comfortable because PostgreSQL uses the spare memory as disk cache. Allow 10 GB of storage, most of which is the container images. For families or several sites, 4 GB or more is recommended. You also need a domain name pointed at the server."

