#~ msgid "If your domain is under duckdns.org, the installer asks early on for your DuckDNS token. <0>Nothing appears on screen as you paste it</0> – the token is hidden, and the installer tells you how many characters it read so you can see the paste landed. If DuckDNS does not accept it you can paste another. Press Enter with nothing pasted and it tells you the address to set yourself in <1>Step 3</1> instead. For any other domain, it prints the two records to create by hand. Either way it keeps working while the server boots, and waits for DNS before it requests certificates."
#~ msgstr "If your domain is under duckdns.org, the installer asks early on for your DuckDNS token. <0>Nothing appears on screen as you paste it</0> – the token is hidden, and the installer tells you how many characters it read so you can see the paste landed. If DuckDNS does not accept it you can paste another. Press Enter with nothing pasted and it tells you the address to set yourself in <1>Step 3</1> instead. For any other domain, it prints the two records to create by hand. Either way it keeps working while the server boots, and waits for DNS before it requests certificates."

