#: ../portal/src/lib/components/docs/PlatformAdminNote.svelte
msgid "Cannot see the Administration section?"
msgstr "Cannot see the Administration section?"

#~ msgid "Administration is only visible to a <0>platform admin</0>. That is a separate permission from a tenant's <1>owner</1> role, so being the owner of your instance is not enough on its own. Opening <2/> without it sends you back to <3>Settings</3>. On a new install the permission goes to the owner of the first tenant, granted when that owner finishes setting up their passkey or sign-in provider. <4/><5/> If you set your instance up on an earlier version, the grant only ran while the API was starting, so the owner never received it. Restart the Nocturne API container once and sign in again. That works as long as nobody currently holds the permission. If someone does, have them grant it to you from <6>Settings > Administration</6>."
#~ msgstr "Administration is only visible to a <0>platform admin</0>. That is a separate permission from a tenant's <1>owner</1> role, so being the owner of your instance is not enough on its own. Opening <2/> without it sends you back to <3>Settings</3>. On a new install the permission goes to the owner of the first tenant, granted when that owner finishes setting up their passkey or sign-in provider. <4/><5/> If you set your instance up on an earlier version, the grant only ran while the API was starting, so the owner never received it. Restart the Nocturne API container once and sign in again. That works as long as nobody currently holds the permission. If someone does, have them grant it to you from <6>Settings > Administration</6>."

#: ../portal/src/lib/components/docs/VerificationSteps.svelte
msgid "Replace <0/> with your <1/>. The bundled Caddy proxy serves HTTPS on ports 80 and 443. The server returns a JSON response with its status. (With a bring-your-own reverse proxy, query the gateway on host port 8080 instead.)"
msgstr "Replace <0/> with your <1/>. The bundled Caddy proxy serves HTTPS on ports 80 and 443. The server returns a JSON response with its status. (With a bring-your-own reverse proxy, query the gateway on host port 8080 instead.)"

#: ../portal/src/lib/components/docs/SystemRequirements.svelte
msgid "<0>Memory.</0> Those six use roughly 1 to 1.5 GB between them at rest, most of it PostgreSQL and the API. 2 GB leaves little spare once the operating system is accounted for, which is why it is the floor rather than a comfortable target. The extra memory at 4 GB is used by PostgreSQL as disk cache and is the single cheapest thing you can give it."
msgstr "<0>Memory.</0> Those six use roughly 1 to 1.5 GB between them at rest, most of it PostgreSQL and the API. 2 GB leaves little spare once the operating system is accounted for, which is why it is the floor rather than a comfortable target. The extra memory at 4 GB is used by PostgreSQL as disk cache and is the single cheapest thing you can give it."

#~ msgid "<0>Storage.</0> The container images account for about 2.5 GB before any data. A single CGM writes roughly 105,000 glucose readings a year, which with indexes and write-ahead logs comes to well under 1 GB per year. 10 GB fits the images and several years of one person's data. 20 GB is for households, longer history, or an imported Nightscout database."
#~ msgstr "<0>Storage.</0> The container images account for about 2.5 GB before any data. A single CGM writes roughly 105,000 glucose readings a year, which with indexes and write-ahead logs comes to well under 1 GB per year. 10 GB fits the images and several years of one person's data. 20 GB is for households, longer history, or an imported Nightscout database."

